From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:54:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: prores: Add the T8132 built-in
 initialization rows

T8132 had no built-in rows, so the M4 encoder bound only when a
per-machine apple/prores-t8132-init.bin was present.

Add the rows macOS 27.2 leaves in the engine before its first ProRes job
on a J604 (MacBook Pro 14" M4), recorded with an MMIO trace of all three
apr windows: 82 SCODEC-system (aux) rows, 80 engine (core) rows and 48
AXI-to-fabric wrapper rows, in the order macOS applies them, which is
also the driver's apply order. The counts match the APRI v1 T8132
layout. As for T6041, each row writes the full register, so the engine
starts from exactly the state macOS programs.

The optional init file still replaces the built-in rows.

Tested on a J604 with the same rows from the file: 30 4K 4:2:2 frames
encode in 85 ms and decode back, no kernel error.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/prores/Kconfig   |   6 +-
 .../platform/apple/prores/apple-prores-drv.c  | 234 +++++++++++++++++-
 .../platform/apple/prores/t6041-apri.rst      |   4 +-
 3 files changed, 238 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/prores/Kconfig b/drivers/media/platform/apple/prores/Kconfig
index 9f2c8e6b07..a1ff582fdf 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/prores/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/prores/Kconfig
@@ -13,9 +13,9 @@ config VIDEO_APPLE_PRORES
 	  (T6050) and A18 Pro (T8140) SoCs. On T8132, T6041 and T6050 a
 	  per-machine apple/prores-t8132-init.bin, -t6041-init.bin or
 	  -t6050-init.bin takes the place of any built-in initialization
-	  rows; none has built-in rows yet, so each needs its file to bind. It encodes 8
-	  and 16 bit 4:2:2 and 4:4:4 frames to ProRes 422 Proxy, LT, 422, HQ,
-	  4444 and 4444 XQ.
+	  rows; T8132 has built-in rows, T6041 and T6050 need their file to
+	  bind. It encodes 8 and 16 bit 4:2:2 and 4:4:4 frames to ProRes 422
+	  Proxy, LT, 422, HQ, 4444 and 4444 XQ.
 
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
 	  will be called apple-prores.
